    "body": "Ah alright\r\nI'm thinking a few things then:\r\n* A new method `Context#get_config_path`\r\n* Would need `Context#new_with_env` for testing since the init of `Context` uses STARSHIP_CONFIG / HOME on `new`\r\n* There is `config.rs#get_config_path` and `configure.rs#get_config_path`. They look practically identical to me, I think they can be consolidated to one definition in a new method `Context#get_config_path`?\r\n\r\nCode in `master` is like this:\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nclassDiagram\r\n`configure.rs#print_configuration` --> `config.rs#StarshipConfig` : in initialize()\r\n`config.rs#StarshipConfig` --> env : config.rs#get_config_path fetches STARSHIP_CONFIG\r\n`context.rs#Context` *-- `config.rs#StarshipConfig` : in new()\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think these ideas are ok if the idea is to have all env mocking in `Context`, what do you think?",
    "created_at": "2023-03-23T11:02:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-23T11:02:36Z",
